{"title":"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(least_computation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (least computation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aed0e713fe306d80a9c40028919c40699fc610b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec x+\\tan x=\\frac{22}7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"143\" height=\"37\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1bced3c72309d8fa6a8c87433a15ddb85724fb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\csc x+\\cot x=\\frac mn,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"145\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b9ffa9646e74f6e94a4a66b824c3a3f08f4f4b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" /> is in lowest terms.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e1e56af09620018654c2779eddeca47211c93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n^{}_{}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identities#Pythagorean_Identities\" title=\"Trigonometric identities\">trigonometric Pythagorean identities</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e5915bda7ef3c2ecdfd4e608567b7946c281b7e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + \\tan^2 x = \\sec^2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b3b506380cec4206c8a8c63c9397a1295d990d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + \\cot^2 x = \\csc^2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>If we square the given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c4c2baf5adcba7fa235c53b7f470678b529507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec x = \\frac{22}{7} - \\tan x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"144\" height=\"37\" />, we find that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f377a54dff224987396113d46dabae23424ca9b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sec^2 x &amp;= \\left(\\frac{22}7\\right)^2 - 2\\left(\\frac{22}7\\right)\\tan x + \\tan^2 x \\\\ 1 &amp;= \\left(\\frac{22}7\\right)^2 - \\frac{44}7 \\tan x \\end{align*}\" width=\"318\" height=\"99\" />\n</p><p>This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf8dd6cf28c814ba9464368dc3fb4e7ceef7830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x = \\frac{435}{308}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/6904831892e4080fb4715c6c052235424f1a8f41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"52\" height=\"33\" />. Then squaring, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16ca781074f142e478d3ca701bf7599dedef1e73.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc^2 x = (y - \\cot x)^2 \\Longrightarrow 1 = y^2 - 2y\\cot x.\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"19\" /> \n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d97cc688df2b20ec301afc53c7d464f046b85b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot x = \\frac{1}{\\tan x} = \\frac{308}{435}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"38\" /> yields a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation\" title=\"Quadratic equation\">quadratic equation</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/2/e8254c921b89f1b057707676294526380c1a540b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = 435y^2 - 616y - 435 = (15y - 29)(29y + 15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"373\" height=\"19\" />. It turns out that only the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> root will work, so the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4ff0e28b4550af010d6fc1955f5f230168463a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{29}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d135a6b7d52d58752efaf6dc379a3cf09d8caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n = \\boxed{044}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Note: The problem is much easier computed if we consider what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71fad852ed694a44a2aea3f188f9645ce3c6f62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec (x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> is, then find the relationship between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d29ce003f41ebb580efb2bb860d6b7e92534373.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin( x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ac0dba333d743e2bb63c61750f018adef5efbd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cos (x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> (using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edd277026286bf7be17926ea388c0dac696217f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan (x) = \\frac{435}{308}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />, and then computing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e000476aa45f0848bc9782b35f884d829aadbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\csc x + \\cot x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" /> using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7bcf7a34f0dfc2818b1b043211a860d1db3001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/\\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> and then the reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d89357bdd19795ccb9fd53b8528e215d4aa860c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x$\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f3a48121a14441106f32cea2c0d15167cff796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec^2 x - \\tan^2 x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" />, from which we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/849041a0c726415d210c6389b9d33dadf171e9f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec x - \\tan x = 7/22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />. Adding the equations\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6ed64ca0c46c61dee09d26b1c3d200307bdced8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\sec x + \\tan x &amp; = &amp; 22/7 \\\\ \\sec x - \\tan x &amp; = &amp; 7/22\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"181\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>together and dividing by 2 gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c8feab2056ae691b25c5495b328d5a396cad066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec x = 533/308$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />, and subtracting the equations and dividing by 2 gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929173fee4372b53570641b0268f374ac572a65f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x = 435/308$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/13264602bd15e96c7c8bfd4a7c0a9b83dcc32822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x = 308/533$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbefd2562527a6268198b73c6b6bc792e4bda7b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x = \\tan x \\cos x = (435/308)(308/533) = 435/533$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"407\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350171e62e6a0efa8afb52a203ec350c6a9e3e72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\csc x = 533/435$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c403b48474625d76c5b7f9f9b8e2826f191e17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot x = 308/435$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. Finally,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e2e2ed43dce843b2c589a29e4715e77ede1dff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc x + \\cot x = \\frac {841}{435} = \\frac {29}{15},\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93caae7dc9f4e5073ce3fcfa46e106e27c9686d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n = 044$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28least_computation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(least_computation)\">Solution 3 (least computation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (least computation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the given,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccd637afc69e6b7c6133a677b456fcc2a59de0f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{\\cos x} + \\frac {\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac {22}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"37\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac10899e7e25ca1043ff2f3b4f22cc8a1694144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{\\sin x} + \\frac {\\cos x}{\\sin x} = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"137\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying the two, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82debef39ea83cd221d382d0dbe3ea2beb4e6ea1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {1}{\\sin x \\cos x} + \\frac {1}{\\sin x} + \\frac {1}{\\cos x} + 1 = \\frac {22}{7}k\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting both of the two given equations from this, and simpliyfing with the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/f/d9ff3aa83911188220c54d113c2153540124d469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\sin x}{\\cos x} + \\frac {\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\frac{\\sin ^2 x + \\cos ^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x} = \\frac {1}{\\sin x \\cos x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"348\" height=\"40\" />, we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fa1a7d9558c4baa08b62fc44f32f7b32e1c3f04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = \\frac {22}{7}k - \\frac {22}{7} - k.\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Solving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7beb1276e5d3c9d18907ef9c441860a9113a0844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac {29}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b56d19efc8dc77bf3e0352dcf3d358b02863e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = 044$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Make the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc26cac424973520a0381fc7f36b4adc5c55a10e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = \\tan \\frac x2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"76\" height=\"33\" /> (a substitution commonly used in calculus). By the half-angle identity for tangent, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05df51b331017f8c418291c599032c972c04b04c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\frac x2 = \\frac{\\sin x}{1+\\cos x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/3945296f7fed0c9c4f16cb78c160566d7680a00e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\csc x + \\cot x = \\frac{1+\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\frac1u = \\frac mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"275\" height=\"37\" />. Also, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb4e2253b8c9639fe94a479f82b3c03985d930a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec x + \\tan x = \\frac{1 + \\sin x}{\\cos x}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"197\" height=\"37\" /> Now note the following:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/023032c4dbcd0e7c5d7a5487516fa31089377aa8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\sin x &amp;= \\frac{2u}{1+u^2}\\\\ \\cos x &amp;= \\frac{1-u^2}{1+u^2}\\end{align*}\" width=\"113\" height=\"85\" />\n</p><p>Plugging these into our equality gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/9520c0d1cd31c6da97be809ad1fb1aff38df180e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1+\\frac{2u}{1+u^2}}{\\frac{1-u^2}{1+u^2}} = \\frac{22}7\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc2a3f72722d1b635b0562f29b41000caffe79d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+u}{1-u} = \\frac{22}7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />, and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc6932b341ac97b7412e7c77b394dfec882cb2c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = \\frac{15}{29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06f6b2b03391431af4c002ea0b4ae4f1eda23a88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac mn = \\frac{29}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b56d19efc8dc77bf3e0352dcf3d358b02863e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = 044$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/8705788ba61468240d06ea592295ef3a81f71a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+\\sin x}{\\cos x}=\\frac{22}7\\implies\\frac{1+\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\cdot\\frac{1-\\sin x}{1-\\sin x}=\\frac{1-\\sin^2x}{\\cos x(1-\\sin x)}=\\frac{\\cos^2x}{\\cos x(1-\\sin x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"614\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85cd2e9b7bf4154831f79d21a1363c2d62270da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{\\cos x}{1-\\sin x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"33\" />, or equivalently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d6100caac08b6648d677416ca9e48b84aba1ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x=\\frac{7+7\\sin x}{22}=\\frac{22-22\\sin x}7\\implies\\sin x=\\frac{22^2-7^2}{22^2+7^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"450\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92f09c927f9b6d64a2e3a5969e75fc6ae89c80b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies\\cos x=\\frac{2\\cdot22\\cdot7}{22^2+7^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"177\" height=\"40\" />. Note that what we want is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5cbb0e28e4dd94198fbda835faa49afedad79a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+\\cos x}{\\sin x}=\\frac{1+\\frac{2\\cdot22\\cdot7}{22^2+7^2}}{\\frac{22^2-7^2}{22^2+7^2}}=\\frac{22^2+7^2+2\\cdot22\\cdot7}{22^2-7^2}=\\frac{(22+7)^2}{(22-7)(22+7)}=\\frac{22+7}{22-7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"588\" height=\"51\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2f32a5426fa316b4ed3a2c5ce165a1a2405d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{29}{15}\\implies m+n=29+15=\\boxed{044}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"286\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assign a right triangle with angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, adjacent side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and opposite side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\nThen, through the given information above, we have that..\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/370b5813c660eecbcbb89575aa23803409942a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{a}+\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{22}{7}\\implies \\frac{c+b}{a}=\\frac{22}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"232\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32fb9165e73fa708ab8fbf723f02933aee9cc0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{b}+\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{m}{n}\\implies \\frac{a+c}{b}=\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"227\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Hence, because similar right triangles can be scaled up by a factor, we can assume that this particular right triangle is indeed in simplest terms.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488bcbbfc44929fdf9b59dd95981d4c76546c72c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b220180a8a46aea12c6768e7304976b8c3cf85c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Furthermore, by the Pythagorean Theorem, we have that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/848f116c1fb78d4bc56c6407f03639d0087d4cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=c^2\\implies 49+b^2=c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> in the first equation and plugging in into the second equation...\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e5be610769c714a74ea27c9f070055ac592000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+b^2=(22-b)^2\\implies 49+b^2=484-44b+b^2\\implies 44b=435\\implies b=\\frac{435}{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"630\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed183433cede5f36e76752d090fa5d44063a5827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=22-\\frac{435}{44}=\\frac{533}{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now, we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c2b001a47198ca2c5423e94181ecc76f882c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+c}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"42\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in, we find the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65dd1abae1bf5fe4fde77e6066bd1cb5c383605a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{7\\cdot{44}}{44}+\\frac{533}{44}}{\\frac{435}{44}}=\\frac{841}{435}=\\frac{29}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"178\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328a24b90c19277bf83235d83d7f0e1adf273a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29+15=\\boxed{044}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/b/eaba3c2bedf4a2e61c7e8fd9ad21759e07be07d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec(x) = \\frac{h}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5fc2cc7e71bd90963ed962f4933856a374153e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x) = \\frac{o}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3eabe6c97f03e413d1aa3c292e9478f286e64df1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o$\" width=\"9\" height=\"8\" /> represent the hypotenuse, adjacent, and opposite (respectively) to angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in a right triangle. Thus we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f389c1c293c7ef61ee73dbac07ad6f018275fe32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec(x) + \\tan(x) = \\frac{h+o}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"189\" height=\"37\" />. We also have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e7076885d706cb36b336690563b6c17bc4e5f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\csc(x) + \\cot(x) = \\frac{h}{o} + \\frac{a}{o} = \\frac{h+a}{o}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"262\" height=\"37\" />. Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec191a9fa7b7bb58094dd4750fc5e14ab4fa270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec(x) + \\tan(x) = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> and csc(x)+cot(x) = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />. Then, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/656e20d94638edb9b6b9d0319b3f621c62f96fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta = \\frac{h+o}{a} + \\frac{h+a}{o} = \\frac{oh+ah+o^2 + a^2}{oa} = \\frac{h(o+a+h)}{oa}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"475\" height=\"39\" /> ( This is because of the Pythagorean Theorem, recall <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd60d70ea4d46cf034ba9ee82058d92adae755e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o^2 +a^2 = h^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />). But then notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d254d656f041803c278db76b4ede8e16ec0ade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha \\cdot \\beta = \\frac{(o+h)(a+h)}{oa} = \\frac{oa +oh +ha +h^2}{oa} = 1+ \\frac{h(o+a+h)}{oa} = 1+ \\alpha + \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"604\" height=\"39\" />. From the information provided in the question, we can substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/458baa8df946d77715f36061b60a5b526a628c07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{22}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/4604297a010816befbb2112f9ff1053b243195c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{22 \\beta}{7}= \\beta + \\frac{29}{7} \\Longrightarrow 22 \\beta = 7 \\beta + 29 \\Longrightarrow 15 \\beta = 29 \\Longrightarrow \\beta = \\frac{29}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"473\" height=\"38\" />. Since, essentially we are asked to find the sum of the numerator and denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2ce12b2e398e3e5b99f79d0c671c13fbeec1ed14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29 + 15 = \\boxed{044}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~qwertysri987\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Firstly, we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a519784ef8a569e3e0c314e6d7a8bfe6ac97dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec x+\\tan x=a/b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351e2f495dedd81ea3ea3485288253dc7b279959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=22$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe4d6ebef2a09e428f2984fb2d677c342dbe1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. This will allow us to spot factorable expressions later. Now, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/3/e6370c478e9d4e7bf0a67e1dda8909462467e47c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec^2x-\\tan^2x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" />, this gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd4665dfc96c318525f4638eaecbf06b7cd4809c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sec x-\\tan x=\\frac{b}{a}\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"37\" /> Adding this to our original expressions gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f911e77d8b4a92bacfe4c5c28b9d9a1f49d3af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sec x=\\frac{a^2+b^2}{ab}\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"39\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb48a01477f60dc5759e82b3630ae394756c643.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos x=\\frac{2ab}{a^2+b^2}\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"39\" /> Now since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3219d16158f4b68175e655cd13eb32fe26ea845c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2x+\\cos^2x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c46b3b4109fd6ea83355a4ff21124247b5d38b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x=\\sqrt{1-\\cos^2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> So we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acfe03ebda383989eaa1d2ed3492f37b092b40b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin x=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{4a^2b^2}{(a^2+b^2)^2}}\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"53\" /> Upon simplification, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2d01983917e1aec63d2805b53890853947aa41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin x=\\frac{a^2-b^2}{a^2+b^2}\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"40\" /> We are asked to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c9721868f1e9706538d2a7cb060ab953fef546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/\\sin x+\\cos x/\\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" /> so we can write that as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/82915636d9ba09643ccf51af861844a7f67eadf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc x+\\cot x=\\frac{1}{\\sin x}+\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/83792a6e9ee28c6708c923c10b6b38d8fb3ddd8c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc x+\\cot x=\\frac{a^2+b^2}{a^2-b^2}+\\frac{2ab}{a^2+b^2}\\frac{a^2+b^2}{a^2-b^2}\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"40\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6deb266ef0c2f1efbfbb9a79615f90d468db040b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc x+\\cot x=\\frac{a^2+b^2+2ab}{a^2-b^2}\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c792f5ca5efa5f9885ec19bed7a16cdb55d94b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc x+\\cot x=\\frac{(a+b)^2}{(a-b)(a+b)}\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39d0744934cb91000ef86469f187ffba5151f6b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc x+\\cot x=\\frac{a+b}{a-b}\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"37\" /> Now using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351e2f495dedd81ea3ea3485288253dc7b279959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=22$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe4d6ebef2a09e428f2984fb2d677c342dbe1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> yields, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed715bd46521075c0dbc941ad6cc51514979a24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc x+\\cot x=\\frac{29}{15}=\\frac{p}{q}\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"41\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/1500b0da4417da2649b27f5710c2a2b13db15969.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q=15+29=\\boxed{44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~Chessmaster20000\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9\">Solution 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewriting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8b92f9e35b42f2b7d8fd6c303a55fd7142ca1b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sec{x}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593e5c9451474d29ad13abf25283cebf82fd6d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{x}$\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41470508df2ceb87f97c7e939589024bceb16e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9cfae39cb378f17672726fb1de7705b94a6da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/7152a652b7eb79c15a97eee69bd1bae7dc1a68e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1+\\sin{x}}{\\cos{x}}=\\frac{22}{7}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Clearing fractions, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa3958b05efcc719e5d30a8739caee5d8963b2cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[22\\cos{x}=7+7\\sin{x}.\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Squaring to get an expression in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc86ca513489e58b10893667e9403b10528c468f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2{x}$\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77950adba3ddd4e093764668f1b69a5e0fb1ae27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2{x}$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962641c5ff16bb538fdcd5837cc838f574c954aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[484\\cos^2{x}=49+49\\sin^2{x}+98\\sin{x}.\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9a4dfb96b698ed085b339ccbe3ff339dbe8b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2{x}=1-\\sin^2{x},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc3c82ccde2ec4d8f01a55838c557db157c5009.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[484(1-\\sin^2{x})=49+49\\sin^2{x}+98\\sin{x}.\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Expanding then collecting terms yields a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b595aa0801cdd3f8f6ba0becd999fac7e2f272a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x}:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a503c648dc4de82fe309d1bd80631d2aee7623cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[533\\sin^2{x}+98\\sin{x}-435=0.\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>To make calculations easier, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9a32aa1a44af414b8dbca813bf74c07101750c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sin{x}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/4344ba4d19c5b866e01ff09c76c733f93bbf8bf5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[533y^2+98y-435=0.\\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Upon inspection, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbab939b716843df7cc6fdb3e9a0b91b2fea5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> is a root. Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/8/7f801b9f0ef3c2c1d614cd42c8abd34ebedf7c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f192b8d3bdfc30a54a9dda6812bdf569ab223b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[533y^2+98y-435=(533y-435)(y+1).\\]\" width=\"326\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a832f312bed91d5e6f95b9c28f2e741ed8be5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sin{x},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e36594238a9f8aa09728ab7c68d36b1b35b1f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x}=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> doesn't work, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0489389191ce7b87b0e2d94792db1284551cc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593e5c9451474d29ad13abf25283cebf82fd6d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{x}$\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" /> undefined. \n</p><p>We conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab723075a3d12cbc602e0ec26b745b26256ac90f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x}=\\frac{435}{533}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/453e5331f0b65f036fe863f9962f4ff1d66ad572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2{x}+\\cos^2{x}=1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a9f8f7df7dc1ef7f440f59afaf35eaa5899e80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos{x}=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{533^2-435^2}{533^2}}.\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5767460a1e0b6c021d985000d3da8034cea084d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\pm \\frac{308}{533}.\\]\" width=\"67\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>After checking via the given equation, we know that only the positive solution works. \n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc8cf94808a0ab9c3e91906f8427274c8e0d41f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc{x}+\\cot{x}=\\frac{1}{\\sin{x}}+\\frac{\\cos{x}}{\\sin{x}}\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff423f429835df8c719ee41750cd29ce42d7bc78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{533}{435}+\\frac{308}{435}\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd1e2327558a93647bf7d4c9b80573c417d12ee5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{29}{15}=\\frac{m}{n}.\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/046890714c4eb44877b599eeafee8468f9c9027f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{044}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"47\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10\">Solution 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e856d072d29adc24104aea6ad9336d30906bb8d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc{x} + \\cot{x} = \\frac{1+\\cos{x}}{\\sin{x}}=\\frac{2\\cos^2{\\frac{x}{2}}}{2\\sin{\\frac{x}{2}}\\cos{\\frac{x}{2}}}=\\cot{\\frac{x}{2}},\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"46\" />\nas well as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd56ebdc60f5d5ed4d8a82339304bcfc9b9a5ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{22}{7}=\\sec{x} + \\tan{x} = \\frac{1+\\sin{x}}{\\cos{x}} = \\frac{(\\sin{\\frac{x}{2}} + \\cos{\\frac{x}{2}})^2}{\\cos^2{\\frac{x}{2}} - \\sin^2{\\frac{x}{2}}}=\\frac{\\sin{\\frac{x}{2}} + \\cos{\\frac{x}{2}}}{\\cos{\\frac{x}{2}} -\\sin{\\frac{x}{2}}} = \\frac{\\cot{\\frac{x}{2}}+1}{\\cot{\\frac{x}{2}}-1}.\\]\" width=\"606\" height=\"47\" />\nSolving this, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/45077f67c0f81799f5c2e891c7acb9bdf11d2dfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{x}=\\frac{29}{15}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" /> Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c0beeed6469a8b84ab1113052552605559ff2a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{044}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"45\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anduran\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME\" title=\"1991 AIME\">1991 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1991 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017182628\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.075 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.097 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 840/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1768/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 90/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\n